NAME
       containers-registries.conf - which container registries podman and skopeo use

SYNOPSIS
       /etc/containers/registries.conf
       /etc/containers/registries.conf.d/*.conf
       ~/.config/containers/registries.conf

DESCRIPTION
       This file (in TOML format) tells podman, buildah and skopeo where to
       look for images whose names have no registry in front (a "short
       name" such as ubi9/ubi), which registries may be reached without
       TLS, and which are blocked. A user's own
       ~/.config/containers/registries.conf replaces the system file for that
       user (rootless podman); files in registries.conf.d add to it.

       Comments start with #. Lists are written in square brackets with
       quoted strings.

SETTINGS
       unqualified-search-registries = ["REGISTRY", ...]
              The registries tried, in order, for a short image name. With
              more than one, podman asks which to use when it runs in a
              terminal (short-name-mode); in scripts, give the full name.

       short-name-mode = "enforcing"|"permissive"|"disabled"
              Whether podman asks (enforcing), picks the first match, or
              never asks.

       [[registry]]
              A table for one registry, with these keys:

              location = "HOST[:PORT][/PATH]"
                     The registry.

              insecure = true|false
                     Allow plain HTTP or a certificate that cannot be
                     checked.

              blocked = true|false
                     Never pull from this registry.

              prefix = "..." and [[registry.mirror]]
                     Match image names and pull through mirrors.

EXAMPLES
       Search only the classroom registry for short names, and allow it
       without TLS checks:

           unqualified-search-registries = ["registry.lab.example.com"]

           [[registry]]
           location = "registry.lab.example.com"
           insecure = true

       Then:

           podman login registry.lab.example.com
           podman search ubi
           podman pull ubi9/ubi

NOTES
       When a task names one registry, write the full image name
       (registry.lab.example.com/ubi9/ubi) and nothing depends on this file.

SEE ALSO
       podman(1), skopeo(1), buildah(1)
